\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Anyway, Sun Cable is planning a $30bn giant solar farm in Australia that could supply electricity to Darwin but also to Singapore via an undersea cable. Since that cable will run through Indonesia, it\u8217 s been a live question (so to speak) whether Indonesia might also tap into the power.}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Well, according to an MoU signed today between Sun Cable and Indonesia\u8217 s minister for energy and mineral resources,  Arifin Tasrif, a formal collaboration will emerge \u8220 to advance opportunities for renewable energy generation and transmission within Indonesia\u8221 .}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Numbers can be a bit inflated around these things, but the two could help spur a \u8220 green industry\u8221  bonanza which would add as much as $US115bn to Indonesia\u8217 s GDP by 2035, the partners say. (In $A, that\u8217 s about $171bn, but in rupee, it\u8217 s 1.6 quadrillion - or a pretty big number).}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 From what we can make of it, Indonesia has identified five key industries from mining and metals processing that could do with some \u8220 green hydrogen\u8221  (ie not made with fossil fuels), to transport and even \u8220 green fertilisers\u8221 .}
{\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24\par}\pard\plain\itap0\s0\fi0\sb200\sa0\aspalpha\aspnum\adjustright\ltrpar\li0\lin0\ri0\rin0\qj\faauto\sl260\slmult0\rtlch\afs24\ltrch\fs24{\rtlch\af2\alang1025\afs24\ltrch\b0\i0\fs20\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033
\loch\af2\dbch\af2\hich\f2\strike0\ulnone\cf2 Sun Cable\u8217 s \u8220 expertise in solar energy generation and long distance transmission\u8221  could play a role. Given Indonesia is reportedly also talking about linking up Australia\u8217 s large lithium reserves with its plans to expand its battery production, we might expect more such ventures.}
